{"ref":"2018.CC47.1","summary":"In accordance with §27-28 of Chapter 27 of the City of Toronto Municipal Code, the Mayor has called a special meeting of City Council to be held at 9:30 a.m. on Thursday, September 13, 2018 in the Council Chamber, Toronto City Hall, 100 Queen Street West, for the following purposes: 1. To discuss the Premier's announcement that, following the decision by the Ontario Superior Court of Justice, the Ontario Government will be reintroducing a bill to reduce the size of Toronto City Council and use Section 33 of the Canadian Charter of Rights and Freedoms to exempt this bill from judicial review. 2. To introduce and enact a confirming by-law for this special meeting.","decided":"City Council on September 13, 2018, adopted the following: 1. City Council express its strong opposition to Bill 31 and the use of the Section 33 of the constitution in this matter. 2. City Council direct the City Solicitor to challenge the legality of Bill 31 through an application in the Courts. 3. City Council instruct the City Solicitor to respond to any proceeding to which the City is named as a party in a manner that supports Council's decision to challenge Bill 5 and Bill 31 and to seek status as a party in any other proceeding that in the opinion of the City Solicitor, in consultation with the City Manager, would support Council's decision to challenge Bill 5 and Bill 31. 4. City Council instruct the City Solicitor to take any further steps necessary consistent with these instructions, in consultation with the City Manager. 5. City Council instruct the City Solicitor to exhaust all legal avenues, including the appeal of any further judicial ruling(s). 6. In the event that a stay of Justice Belobaba's Order is granted by the Court, City Council request the Province to file Regulations to address the loss of candidates' ability to file nominations with the City Clerk between September 10 to 14, 2018. 7. City Council request the Federal Government to exercise 